{% if system -%}
Select passages that directly support findings for one section of an evidence brief.
Write the exact subject requested by the heading and brief topic together in section_subject before selecting passages.
Resolve ambiguous words using the brief topic. Use the supplied section guidance and sibling headings to determine
which facts belong here. Ignore writing style instructions for this selection.
Choose passages that actually describe the requested subject, including any required setting, population, version or
timeframe. In subject_line give the line number establishing who or what that passage actually describes.
Use the document fields alongside the passage to establish what it describes. If a field conflicts with the assigned subject, use a finding only when the passage explicitly attributes it to the requested subject. A catalogue label alone does not establish a finding.
Select line 0 when its title establishes the exact subject.
For example, a brief about orders placed after a ban cannot use findings about delayed orders unless the source
establishes they were placed after the ban. A common word in the heading and a passage is insufficient.
In finding_lines give the source line numbers, starting from 1, for distinct relevant observations, specific cases
or measurements. Include a line with mixed material if it contains an observation that can stand on its own in this
section. Include a specific example when it provides detail the more general findings lack.
Look for evidence covering every part the assignment asks about. Keep additional passages when they add a different
observation or material detail. Do not stop at the first good source if other passages cover parts it leaves out.
Order the selected passages by direct relevance to the assignment. Include only labels printed in the evidence.
Return a JSON object with section_subject followed by passages. Each passage has citation, subject_line and finding_lines.
If none directly support the assignment, return the section_subject with "passages":[]. Do not draft the section.
{%- else -%}
Assignment: {{ assignment | tojson }}
{% if target_words %}
The finished section aims for about {{ target_words }} words. Select enough distinct relevant evidence for this length
when it is available.
{% endif %}

{% if earlier_text %}
The previous draft cites these passage numbers. Select the exact lines establishing its findings where they are available and relevant, alongside evidence for developing the section. The draft is a set of notes and cannot itself establish a fact.
Previous draft: {{ earlier_text | tojson }}
{% endif %}
Passages:
{{ evidence | safe }}

{% if issues -%}
Fix these problems with the previous selection: {{ issues | tojson }}.
The subject already identified for this section is {{ subject | tojson }}. Keep it while correcting the excerpts.
{% endif -%}
Available labels: {{ allowed_labels | tojson }}
Return only JSON in this form: {"section_subject":"requested subject","passages":[{"citation":4,"subject_line":0,"finding_lines":[1,3]}]}.
{%- endif %}
